docs(release): land M7 quality bar (integration tests + benches + docs + CHANGELOG)

* Integration tests: new `crates/corx-server/tests/integration_proxy.rs`
  drives a fully assembled `axum` router against a `wiremock` upstream
  via `tower::ServiceExt::oneshot`. Coverage spans liveness/readiness,
  CORS preflight short-circuit, end-to-end body forwarding, hostname
  SSRF blocking, origin denial and forwarded-header injection. The
  `MetricsHandle` now exposes `for_test()` so multiple test cases can
  spin up fresh `ServerBuild`s without conflicting on the
  process-wide `metrics` recorder.
* Criterion benchmarks: `crates/corx-core/benches/url_parser.rs` and
  `crates/corx-core/benches/ssrf_guard.rs` cover the two hot-path
  primitives (URL extraction, IP literal SSRF check) so a regression
  shows up as a clear percentage delta.
* Documentation set under `docs/`:
  - `getting-started.md` -- install + first request walkthrough.
  - `configuration.md` -- TOML schema + hot-swappable vs immutable.
  - `security.md` -- defence-in-depth diagram + SSRF / CORS / mTLS.
  - `observability.md` -- log fields, full Prometheus catalogue, OTLP.
  - `operations.md` -- probes, signals, hot reload, capacity knobs.
  - `deployment.md` -- Docker / compose / Helm / TLS / FIPS / CI.
  - `architecture.md` -- workspace layout + request lifecycle diagram.
  - `migration.md` -- breaking-change guide for 0.1 -> 0.2.
  - `testing.md` -- unit + integration + criterion + lint commands.
  - `README.md` -- index across all of the above.
* `CHANGELOG.md` documents every M1-M7 deliverable and the breaking
  changes that come with the workspace split.
* Top-level `README.md` reshaped: highlights now reflect the
  enterprise feature set, CLI subcommands documented, doc table links
  out to the new operator guides.

80 tests passing across the workspace under `--all-features`
(56 corx-core unit + 17 corx-server unit + 7 integration).
